TASK: COMPLETE THE OX-DX TUI EXPERIENCE AND ASSET SYSTEM v1.0

Repository:

https://github.com/bjo163/universal-ontology-engine

Brand:

# OX-DX

Descriptor:

**Universal Ontology & Experience Engine**

Technical implementation:

**Universal Ontology Engine**

Primary:

**FROM STRUCTURE TO EXPERIENCE.**

Secondary:

**FROM UNIVERSE TO BIT.**

Core:

**EVIDENCE FIRST.**

# ============================================================ 0. SCOPE — TUI ONLY

This phase is ONLY for the OX-DX Terminal User Interface.

Do NOT work on:

- desktop GUI
- web GUI
- website
- Next.js
- Vercel
- mobile
- general application UI

Do NOT create a generic "terminal theme".

Build a complete OX-DX TUI experience specification and supporting asset system.

The TUI must be usable as the future visual/interaction foundation for:

- terminal CLI
- ontology inspection
- graph inspection
- evidence inspection
- repository discovery
- source inspection
- runtime observation
- resolution navigation
- diagnostics
- certification/query surfaces

\============================================================

1. CORE TUI IDENTITY
   \============================================================

The TUI should feel like:

**AN INSTRUMENT FOR INSPECTING COMPLEX SYSTEMS.**

Not:

a dashboard

not:

a hacker movie

not:

a terminal clone of a web app

not:

a generic IDE

Core experience:

**SEE → TRACE → RESOLVE**

Secondary:

**OBSERVE → CONNECT → VERIFY**

Primary emotional qualities:

precise
quiet
dense when necessary
technical
raw
focused
slightly mysterious

# ============================================================ 2. TUI DESIGN EQUATION

Use this as the design philosophy:

**MONOSPACE**
\+
**SPATIAL STRUCTURE**
\+
**EVIDENCE**
\+
**RESOLUTION**
\+
**CONTROLLED IMPERFECTION**

Do NOT interpret "grunge" as visual dirt everywhere.

Use:

clean geometry
\+
slightly disturbed surfaces

# ============================================================ 3. REQUIRED DELIVERABLE

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/`

and a complete TUI specification.

Create a master document:

`assets/documentation/OX-DX-TUI-SYSTEM-v1.0.md`

This becomes the authoritative TUI design reference.

# ============================================================ 4. TERMINAL BRAND FOUNDATION

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/tui-brand.md`

Define:

brand mark usage
terminal wordmark
prompt identity
banner identity
status identity
startup identity
shutdown identity

The terminal should be recognizable as OX-DX before the user sees the full command output.

# ============================================================ 5. STARTUP EXPERIENCE

Design an OX-DX terminal startup sequence.

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/startup-experience.md`

Do NOT create a huge ASCII logo.

Use a restrained startup.

Concept:

signal
→
identity
→
system state
→
ready

Example conceptual rhythm:

OX-DX

Universal Ontology & Experience Engine

[ ontology 1.0.0 ]
[ engine ready ]
[ evidence-first mode ]

READY.

Create the actual wording based on repository truth.

Do not invent status values.

# ============================================================ 6. PROMPT LANGUAGE

Define:

`assets/documentation/tui/prompt-language.md`

Design a recognizable terminal prompt.

It should communicate:

context
scope
current location
resolution
state

Avoid copying:

bash
zsh
fish
starship

Create a distinct OX-DX prompt composition.

Example conceptual structure:

[OX-DX]
scope
level
context

>

Do NOT use this exact format automatically.

Develop an original but practical prompt.

# ============================================================ 7. TERMINAL LAYOUT SYSTEM

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/layout-system.md`

Define layouts for:

80×24
100×30
120×40
160×50+

At minimum:

COMPACT
STANDARD
INSPECTION
WIDE
FULL-DEPTH

Each must define:

primary area
secondary area
status area
command area
context area

# ============================================================ 8. OX-DX TERMINAL FRAMING

Do not simply use:

┌───────────────┐
│ title │
├───────────────┤

everywhere.

Develop a distinctive framing language.

Use OX-DX visual grammar:

broken boundaries
partial frames
measurement marks
resolution indicators
context lines
controlled asymmetry

But keep it terminal-safe.

# ============================================================ 9. BORDER SYSTEM

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/border-system.md`

Define:

primary border
secondary border
focus border
observation border
warning border
unknown border
disabled border

Provide:

Unicode form
ASCII fallback

# ============================================================ 10. LINE / SEPARATOR SYSTEM

Define:

`assets/documentation/tui/separator-system.md`

Create a small reusable language:

structural separator
context separator
resolution separator
trace separator
warning separator

Avoid arbitrary decorative separators.

# ============================================================ 11. TERMINAL GLYPH SYSTEM

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/glyph-system.md`

Define glyphs for:

structure
relation
trace
observation
resolution
signal
unknown
warning
verified
error
focus
selected
collapsed
expanded

For every glyph provide:

Unicode
ASCII fallback
meaning
usage
minimum terminal support assumptions

Do not assume all terminals support advanced symbols.

# ============================================================ 12. ANSI COLOR SYSTEM

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/ansi-color-system.md`

Map the canonical OX-DX palette to:

ANSI 8-color
ANSI 16-color
256-color
Truecolor

Define fallback behavior.

Important:

The TUI must remain readable even in:

black and white
low-color terminals
accessibility/high-contrast mode

Do not depend on truecolor.

# ============================================================ 13. COLOR SEMANTICS

Define restrained semantic use:

BASE
STRUCTURE
FOCUS
OBSERVATION
SIGNAL
WARNING
ERROR
UNKNOWN
VERIFIED

Do not assign unsupported technical meaning to colors.

Do not use color as the only status mechanism.

# ============================================================ 14. TEXT HIERARCHY

Define:

TITLE
SECTION
PRIMARY
SECONDARY
METADATA
TECHNICAL
SOURCE
PROVENANCE
STATUS
COMMAND
ERROR
WARNING
UNKNOWN

Keep hierarchy readable in plain ANSI terminal output.

# ============================================================ 15. CURSOR LANGUAGE

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/cursor-system.md`

Define:

default cursor
focus cursor
selection cursor
resolution cursor
input cursor

The cursor should indicate:

where the user is

not:

what the data means

# ============================================================ 16. FOCUS LANGUAGE

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/focus-system.md`

Focus should be visually obvious without overwhelming the screen.

Use:

density
border
marker
inversion
spacing

rather than bright neon everywhere.

# ============================================================ 17. SELECTION LANGUAGE

Define:

`assets/documentation/tui/selection-system.md`

Distinguish:

focused
selected
expanded
active
visited

Do not collapse all states into one highlight.

# ============================================================ 18. RESOLUTION NAVIGATION

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/resolution-navigation.md`

The 49 ontology levels must become a recognizable TUI interaction.

The user should always know:

current level
higher level
lower level
neighboring levels
available evidence

The interface should support:

move
inspect
expand
collapse
zoom/resolution shift
return

Do not treat levels as mandatory filesystem nesting.

# ============================================================ 19. 49-LEVEL COMPACT MODE

Create a compact visualization of:

01 UNIVERSE
...
49 BIT

It must work in narrow terminals.

Possible approaches:

vertical rail
horizontal ticker
compact indexed list

Choose the strongest design.

Do not invent new ordering.

# ============================================================ 20. 49-LEVEL DEEP MODE

Design a full inspection view.

Show:

level number
level name
context
related evidence
relationships
provenance where available

Only display descriptions supported by canonical specification.

# ============================================================ 21. EVIDENCE VIEW

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/evidence-view.md`

Define a source-first surface.

Priority:

native evidence
classification
relation
provenance
interpretation

The source should never be visually lost behind interpretation.

# ============================================================ 22. SOURCE VIEW

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/source-view.md`

Define display for:

file
path
source
line
column
span
native syntax kind

Do not treat source location as identity.

# ============================================================ 23. PROVENANCE VIEW

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/provenance-view.md`

Show:

where
when
context
source

Keep it clearly separate from identity.

# ============================================================ 24. GRAPH VIEW

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/graph-view.md`

Design a terminal-native graph.

Requirements:

focused node
neighbors
relationship
direction
path
context
resolution

Do not attempt to reproduce a GUI node graph literally.

Use spatial text topology.

# ============================================================ 25. GRAPH FOCUS

Define keyboard-driven graph exploration.

Possible concepts:

center
expand
collapse
trace
path
neighbor
parent
child

Verify terms against ontology semantics.

Do not use "parent" when the relationship is not actually structural parentage.

# ============================================================ 26. TRACE VIEW

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/trace-view.md`

Trace should show:

source
relationship
observation
path
resolution

Make trace visually distinct from ownership.

# ============================================================ 27. OBSERVATION VIEW

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/observation-view.md`

Canonical principle:

**OBSERVATION IS NOT OWNERSHIP.**

An execution or observation should be visibly separate from structure.

# ============================================================ 28. UNKNOWN VIEW

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/unknown-view.md`

Unknown must not look like error.

Use:

absence
open boundary
partial trace
quiet marker

Do not use constant flashing.

# ============================================================ 29. VERIFICATION VIEW

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/verification-view.md`

Verification should feel:

stable
settled
precise

Avoid celebratory animation.

# ============================================================ 30. DIAGNOSTICS

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/diagnostics.md`

Define:

info
notice
warning
error
fatal

Each must have:

symbol
text treatment
priority
screen behavior

# ============================================================ 31. ERROR SYSTEM

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/error-system.md`

Errors must state:

what happened
where
why if known
what evidence remains
what can be done next

Never hide malformed input.

Prefer:

"Malformed input observed."

over:

"Something went wrong."

# ============================================================ 32. LOADING SYSTEM

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/loading-system.md`

Define:

DISCOVERING
INSPECTING
PARSING
MAPPING
TRACING
RESOLVING
VERIFYING

No fake percentages.

No infinite noisy spinner.

Provide a static fallback.

