# ============================================================ 37. DENSITY MODES

Define:

LOW
MEDIUM
HIGH
INSPECTION

Rules:

LOW:
thinking / orientation

MEDIUM:
normal use

HIGH:
technical inspection

INSPECTION:
maximum evidence density

# ============================================================ 38. SMALL TERMINAL MODE

At 80×24 or smaller:

prioritize:

context
current object
level
primary evidence
status
navigation

Hide secondary information.

Allow on-demand inspection.

# ============================================================ 39. LARGE TERMINAL MODE

At wider sizes reveal:

graph
provenance
trace
metadata
secondary evidence

Never simply enlarge everything.

# ============================================================ 40. KEYBOARD SYSTEM

Create:

`assets/documentation/tui/keymap.md`

Define:

navigation
selection
focus
resolution
graph
trace
expand
collapse
help
quit

Avoid unnecessary key conflicts.

If current CLI/TUI already has conventions, preserve them.

# ============================================================ 41. VI-STYLE OPTIONALITY

If using:

j / k
h / l

define them as optional navigation shortcuts.

Do not make vi behavior mandatory.

Ensure arrow-key access exists.

# ============================================================ 42. MOUSE SUPPORT

Document optional mouse interaction.

Mouse should supplement:

keyboard

not replace it.

Possible:

click
scroll
drag if genuinely useful

Do not require mouse.

# ============================================================ 43. TUI SOUND

Integrate with the OX-DX Sensory Brand System.

Default:

SILENT

Optional:

MINIMAL

Alerts:

NOTIFY

Never beep for routine navigation.

Map only meaningful events.

# ============================================================ 44. VISUAL MOTION

Use only terminal-compatible motion:

cursor movement
line reveal
small state changes
focus transitions

Avoid:

screen clearing
rapid flashing
fake hacker effects

Respect reduced motion.

# ============================================================ 45. TERMINAL ANIMATION FRAMES

Create examples for:

resolve
trace
scan
verify

Use text/ANSI animation frames.

Store specifications under:

`assets/documentation/tui/animation-frames/`

Do not create high-overhead effects.

